this is a great story to not only  communicate to you things going on in  the real world but also to talk about  how narratives are created and framed by  corporate media  so listen basically support for  impeaching Donald Trump went up when  news of the Ukraine fiasco first broke  hitting about 46 47 percent and then  throughout everything that we've seen  happen publicly related to Ukraine and  Trump so far  if support for impeachment has crept up  to 50 percent 52 percent fifty five  percent depending on which poll you look  at now that by itself is big news this  is a lot more impeachment support than  there was for Richard Nixon early in  Watergate it's not normal when it comes  to previous presidents Obama Bush as  much as Obama and Bush were hated by the  right and left respectively you didn't  have more than half the country saying  that the president should be impeached  when it was Obama and Bush so now we  have a new poll the poll happens to be  from Fox News of all places and it says  indeed 54% of the country wants Donald  Trump impeached now you might notice  that I'm leaving out a piece of  information here and I did it on purpose  for the for the purposes of our story  today I did this deliberately  when I say 54% of the country wants  Trump impeached if you are a media  literate individual if you're a savvy  thinker you should be saying does david  mean 54% want trump impeached by the  house or is david saying 54% want trump  impeached and removed via a conviction  in the senate that is the right question  to be asking and that is exactly the  game that is being played with these  numbers the game that's being played in  lots of corporate media is that they  aren't specifying it clearly whether by  impeachment people understand that to  mean or are meaning to say that they  want the house to impeach and a trial in  the senate whose outcome could be one  thing or the other thing or are people  saying when they say they want to  impeach we want trump 